          <details>
            <summary>How do I calculate 30% off?</summary>
            <p>Multiply the original price by 0.70. For example, a $50 product with 30% off costs $50 × 0.70 = $35.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Is discount applied before tax?</summary>
            <p>Yes. In most retail systems, discounts are applied to the base item price before sales tax or VAT is added.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>How to find original price from sale price?</summary>
            <p>Divide the sale price by (1 - Discount Percentage / 100). For example, if a sale price is $80 after 20% off: $80 / 0.80 = $100 original price.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
